          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bd483cb5d24445e0c05f3baede621e1f7f7f8ac5",
          "message": "zk: add a revealed signature mode to the V5 eddsa-rdfc-2022 relation (#6787)\n\nPolicy::signature_mode selects what the proof hides. Hidden (the default)\nkeeps today's proof of knowledge of each issuer signature. Revealed drops\nsignatures from the witness; the guest commits each credential's\nverification method and eddsa-rdfc-2022 signing input, and the verifier\nchecks the presented signatures outside the proof via\nverify_revealed_with_artifact. The mode is framed into the policy digest\nonly when revealed, so hidden-mode digests are unchanged. The vcq adapter\naccepts only hidden mode.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019QrHZ34TTVfgvvQxbPEKf7\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-10T17:09:19Z",
